  "description": "redundancy.v1 §2.5 to §2.11: one candidate own of a governed interface, its election, and the events its runtime hands it in order -> the step each returns, and its role after the last. Events: \"start\" (begin: claim before reading); \"finish\" (the act the last claim, take_over or step_down asked for is done); {\"read\": R} (the read a read step asked for, R as elections.json writes one); {\"appeared\": id} (its watch heard that instance's interface token appear); \"withdrawn\" (its watch heard the address's interface tokens withdrawn, none left held); \"timer\" (the timer the last step armed fired: the retry interval, or the grace); {\"lock\": bool} (under external, the lock taken or lost). Steps: {\"step\": \"claim\"} (put the descriptor marked standby, declare the instance token and the watch, then finish); {\"step\": \"read\"}; {\"step\": \"grace\"} (arm the grace timer); {\"step\": \"stand_by\", \"why\", \"instance\"?, \"retry\"} (stand by; arm the retry timer when retry; why as elections.json's, or no_lock; retry is false for incumbent and no_lock, true otherwise); {\"step\": \"take_over\"} (core §8.2's order, then finish); {\"step\": \"step_down\", \"why\": \"lower_holder\" with instance, or \"lock_lost\"} (the reverse order, then finish); {\"step\": \"nothing\"}. The machine: start, once, is claim; finish of the claim campaigns (a read, or under external without the lock stand_by no_lock); a read while campaigning decides as elections.json (under external without the lock, stand_by no_lock), take_over or stand_by; finish of a take_over serves, then under external without the lock steps down lock_lost, under claim with an appearance heard while taking over reads (the heal's first read), else nothing; while serving under claim, another instance's appearance reads; that read's holders, own counted whether it shows own or not, two or more arm the grace, else back to serving; the timer reads again; that read's holders, own counted, decide as heals.json with the first read's: step down lower_holder, or back to serving; finish of a step_down stands by, and campaigns when a withdrawal was heard while stepping down, else nothing; while standing by, a withdrawal campaigns (under external only with the lock), a timer campaigns only when the stand_by armed retry; under external, a lock taken while standing by campaigns, a lock lost while serving steps down lock_lost, otherwise it is only remembered. Every other event in every other state is nothing, and changes nothing. role: \"unclaimed\" before the claim's finish, \"standby\" while campaigning, standing by or taking over, \"serving\" while serving, healing or stepping down."
}
